  "register": "notes",
  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\n___\n\nChief Complaint:\nabd pain, diarrhea, N/V\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nMs. ___ is a ___ year old F w/ metastatic pancreatic cancer \nto\nher lung and liver on FOLFIRINOX cycle 2 (start date ___,\nlast dose of chemo ___ presenting with nausea, vomiting,\nabdominal pain, and diarrhea since last night. She has been\nunable to take PO. No recent travel or eating unusual foods. No\nheadaches, fevers, CP, SOB, cough, or dysuria. She had been\nfeeling fatigue two days ago, but then yesterday developed \nsevere\nabdominal pain, nausea, and frequent watery bowel movements \nwhich\nsent her to the hospital. Denies fevers, new foods, sick\ncontacts, recent abx courses. She has had about 8 lbs of weight\nloss due to not eating much from her mouth sores. \n\nIn the ED, vitals were within normal limits. Exam was benign.\nLabs notable for a leukocytosis, anemia, thrombocytopenia, and\nelevated alk phos. CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast showed known\npancreatic adenocarcinoma encasing the splenic artery and vein\nleading to a large splenic infarct, and multiple hepatic lesions\nconcerning for mets. It also showed free fluid in the pelvis. \nCXR\nwas negative. UA was non-inflammatory. She received IV Zofran, \nIV\nmorhine, viscous lidocaine, and 2L NS. \n\nUpon arrival to the floor, the patient has to leave the \ninterview\nto vomit and have liquid diarrhea. She returns and tells the\nabove story. No black or red stools or nausea.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\nMs. ___ is a ___ year old F w/ metastatic pancreatic cancer \nto\nher lung and liver on FOLFIRINOX cycle 2 (start date ___,\nlast dose of chemo ___ presenting with nausea, vomiting,\nabdominal pain, and diarrhea\n\nTRANSITIONAL ISSUES\n===================\n-Continue to evaluate need for tube feeds.\n-Assess need for repeat paracentesis as an outpatient.\n\nACUTE PROBLEMS:\n===============\n# Diarrhea\nConcerning for side effect from Irinotecan given lack of fevers\nor leukocytosis. Ddx also includes c. diff, norovirus given\nvomiting, foodborne illness, or viral gastroenteritis but \ninfectious work up negative. Improved with loperamide 4 mg TID. \n\n# Nausea/vomiting: Likely ___ chemotherapy effects vs. pressure \nfrom significant\nascites vs. intolerance of PO intake, improved with Zofran and \nprochlorperazine. \n\n#Ascites: SAAG 2.7, c/w portal HTN. patient with moderate\nincrease in ascites on interval imaging. Is likely contributing\nto patient nausea and abd d/c. Paracentesis ___ with 650 cc \noff, SAAG 2.7 c/w portal HTN. Some improvement in symptoms but \nrapid reaccumulation of ascites, requiring repeat paracentesis \non ___ with 2L. She may need a repeat tap as an outpatient. \n\n#Nutrition: patient with persistent weight loss, inability to\ntolerate PO. Initiated cycled tube feeds following discussion \nwith with Dr. ___ patient tolerated. \n\n# Abdominal pain: Abdominal CT shows her tumor burden and portal \nvein thrombus. Responded to Tylenol 1g PO q8h and prn PO \ndilaudid, with intermittent requirement of IV Dilaudid. \n\n# Mucositis: responded well to mouthwash and nystatin for thrush \n\n\n# Fatigue: Started a trial of dexamethasone 1 mg every morning \nstarting on\nday 4 of cycle. Per Dr. ___ her anxiety and \nsignificant energy, we dose reduced to 0.5mg daily.\n\n# Metastatic pancreatic cancer on FOLFIRINOX cycle 2 (start date \n___,\nlast dose of FOLFIRNOX C3D1 ___: CT scan shows reduction in \nprimary tumor burden. Pt and her family are having a very \ndifficult time coping and still are\nhoping for a cure. SW and palliative care consulted. \n\n# Portal vein thrombus: Continued home apixaban\n\n# GERD: Continued home PPI and H2 blocker. Continued simethicone\n\n# Pancreatic insufficiency: Continued home Creon with meals and \nsnacks\n\n# Hypothyroidism: we continued home levothyroxine",
